    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0309" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 411.57N83/191a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-12T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5792. For McCormick:</p>
                <p>5. <hi rendition="#italic">Norway</hi>. We think agreement with British for
                    division of Norwegian tonnage should be made before initiating suggested
                    negotiations with Norway.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Denmark</hi>. We think it improbable that Danish
                    negotiations can be protracted much longer without complete rupture and if we
                    are not to proceed with these negotiations here to final conclusion without
                    delay then we think Danes should be frankly informed that negotiations are
                    transferred to London. War Trade Board.</p>
                <p>For McCormick from Polk:</p>
                <p>In regard to above message feel it necessary that we should state to
                    representatives of Danish Government here that negotiations have been delayed
                    and transferred in compliance with wishes of French and British Governments.
                    This important in order to prevent this Government from being charged with bad
                    faith. Please cable your views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
